{
  "about": "The demo's cut (SPRINT-OCT24 6.2), segment by segment: what each shows, the steps walk.mjs takes on it, and its voice line, which starts at the segment's {\"mark\": \"voice\"} step, once its screen shows what the line says. cut.py fills {open} (rb open's address), serves the two casts as /files/pain.cast and /files/import.cast, and runs it. Every voice line must match what the segment's screen shows on the demo record (D4); rb_open_today is the dry run on rb open as it is, shell the A+ shell (rb open's own /, no test switch). A voice may be one line per mode where the screens differ. Ids in steps (c-c-pt-1024, [data-rcpt], runxhzv6x) are the demo record's (take 4). A step marked \"lead\" runs before filming starts (the shell's pointer guide set seen). A cast segment, which drops no marker, may say when its line starts with \"voice_at\" (seconds into it). A segment's \"zoom\" frames the part its voice speaks of, at 1.5 to 2 times: a box [x, y, w, h] in the walk's CSS pixels (the frame's shape, inside the frame, never under 720 wide), per mode where the segment has steps per mode. It eases in over 0.4 s to be full when the voice starts and eases out after the line ends; a {\"mark\": \"subject\", \"rect\": ...} step keeps where the part the voice speaks of is drawn, and the cut refuses a box that leaves it out, or the cursor.",
